%N A402265 Indices m for which the sum of the first m abundant numbers A173107(m) is itself abundant.
%C A402265 A173107(277) = 159075 is the least odd abundant number in A173107, so 277 is the smallest term that produces the first odd abundant number in A173107.
%C A402265 The analogous sequence for deficient numbers is A402266.
%F A402265 Integers m such that A173107(m) = A401272(m).
%e A402265 A173107(1) = 12 that is abundant, so 1 is a term.
%e A402265 A173107(2) = 30 that is abundant, so 2 is a term.
%e A402265 A173107(3) = 50 that is deficient, so 3 is not a term.
%t A402265 Position[Accumulate[Select[Range[500], DivisorSigma[-1, #] > 2 &]], _?(DivisorSigma[-1, #] > 2 &)] // Flatten (* _Amiram Eldar_, Nov 16 2026 *)
